 html←{levels}DemoteHeadings html;pat;rep;old;new
⍝ Shifts every heading in `html` down by `levels`, which defaults to 1. H6 stays as it is,
⍝ because there is nowhere further to go.
⍝ A README starts at H1, which on a page that has an H1 and an H2 of its own would compete
⍝ with both. The caller decides how far down it has to go; see `RenderReadme`.
⍝ One ⎕R with a pattern per level rather than one pass per level: ⎕R does not rescan what it
⍝ has replaced, so H1 cannot be shifted to H2 by the first pattern and on to H3 by the next.
 levels←{0<⎕NC ⍵:⍎⍵ ⋄ 1}'levels'
 old←'123456'
 new←6⌊levels+⍳6
 pat←((⊂'<h'),¨old),(⊂'</h'),¨old
 rep←((⊂'<h'),¨⍕¨new),(⊂'</h'),¨⍕¨new
 html←pat ⎕R rep⍠('IC' 1)⊣html
⍝Done
